---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Developer Roadmap Library"
  description="Read the Privacy Policy for Roadmap Library. Learn how we handle local progress data, display advertisements, analytics, and user privacy rights."
>
  <div class="container section-sm" style="max-width: 900px;">
    <span class="text-caption-mono" style="color: var(--color-mute);">Legal & Compliance</span>
    <h1 class="text-display-lg" style="margin: 8px 0 12px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-body-md" style="color: var(--color-mute); margin-bottom: 32px;">Last Updated: August 8, 2026</p>

    <div class="seo-article-body" style="color: var(--color-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 28px;">
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        At <strong>Roadmap Library</strong> (accessible from <a href="https://roadmaplibrary.com" style="color: var(--color-link);">roadmaplibrary.com</a>), one of our main priorities is the privacy of our visitors. This Privacy Policy document outlines the types of information that is collected and recorded by Roadmap Library and how we use it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin: 32px 0 16px;">1. Browser Local Storage Data</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Roadmap Library operates as a privacy-focused interactive application. Your roadmap progress (such as checked topic boxes and preferred view modes) is saved locally in your browser using standard <code>localStorage</code> technology. This progress data remains strictly on your personal device and is never transmitted, stored, or sold to remote databases.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin: 32px 0 16px;">2. Log Files</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Roadmap Library follows a standard procedure of using log files. These files log visitors when they visit websites. Web hosting companies collect standard data including internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date and time stamp, referring/exit pages, and possibly the number of clicks. These are not linked to any information that is personally identifiable. The purpose of the information is for analyzing trends, administering the site, tracking users' movement on the website, and gathering demographic information.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin: 32px 0 16px;">3. Display Advertising & Cookies</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Roadmap Library displays third-party ad banners (such as Google AdSense) to keep our educational resources free for all users worldwide.
      </p>
      <ul style="margin-bottom: 24px; padding-left: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;">
        <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to our website or other websites.</li>
        <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visit to our sites and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
        <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-link);">Google Ads Settings</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin: 32px 0 16px;">4. Third-Party Web Links</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Our interactive roadmaps contain outbound links to official documentation, educational articles, and third-party tutorials. Roadmap Library has no control over and assumes no responsibility for the content, privacy policies, or practices of any third-party sites or services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin: 32px 0 16px;">5. GDPR & CCPA Data Protection Rights</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        We would like to make sure you are fully aware of all of your data protection rights. Every user is entitled to the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing, object to processing, and data portability. Because Roadmap Library does not collect personal user accounts or store personal identification data on remote servers, no user identification profiles exist on our infrastructure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink); margin: 32px 0 16px;">6. Contact Us About Privacy</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        If you have additional questions or require more information about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us through our <a href="/contact" style="color: var(--color-link);">Contact Page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
